We've spent the last two weeks testing "FlowTask," the new project management tool that's been getting a lot of buzz. The user interface is absolutely beautiful; it's clean, intuitive, and our team was able to onboard in less than an hour. The real-time collaboration features are also top-notch. Seeing tasks update instantly across the team is a game-changer for our workflow.

However, the glowing praise stops when you look at the price. At $50 per user per month, it is shockingly expensive. This is double what competitors like Asana or Monday charge. We also ran into a critical bug that prevented us from exporting our final reports. We contacted customer support, and it took them three full days to send a single, unhelpful reply.

Furthermore, the mobile app is a complete disaster. It's sluggish, crashes constantly, and is missing key features from the desktop version, making it useless for our team members in the field.

In conclusion, FlowTask has a brilliant UI and great core ideas, but its crippling price, non-existent support, and broken mobile app make it impossible to recommend. We'll be sticking with our old system for now.